  "notes": "Instance settings (type, AMI, EBS encryption, IMDSv2, user data) are accepted either on the instance or in a launch template. The 'only' checks (sg_in_not_world, sg_in_only_web_ports, sg_out_only_https_range) read the group the instance or launch template references, so a second, unrelated group does not fail them. Separate rule resources can't be bound to a group alongside 'all', so those branches apply to every such rule; sg_in_not_world's branch only rejects a world-open source, to allow a rule for an unrelated group."
}
